// Automatic updates (unattended-upgrades) also install FlickOS's own packages
// and the community apps: this adds FlickOS's two distributions to the origins
// that Debian's 50unattended-upgrades allows. Shipped by
// flickos-archive-keyring, with the repository itself
// (sources.list.d/flickos.sources); origin, codename and label are the
// distributions' own (repo/conf/distributions). Community apps update this
// way because every version is built from public source, checked and
// reviewed before it is signed (Software design, Q10).
//
// Settings > Updates (flickos-control) replaces the whole list in
// 60flickos-updates when a choice is made there, so this file then no longer
// counts; "Security fixes only" leaves FlickOS out.
Unattended-Upgrade::Origins-Pattern {
        "origin=FlickOS,codename=${distro_codename},label=FlickOS";
        "origin=FlickOS,codename=${distro_codename}-community,label=FlickOS Community";
};
